%% Lightning Invoice Creation Flow
%% PAY-018: Payment Flow Mermaid Diagrams
%%
%% This sequence diagram shows the complete flow for creating a
%% Lightning Network BOLT11 invoice from user request to database storage.
%%
%% Key Steps:
%% 1. User initiates payment request
%% 2. API validates and authenticates
%% 3. Lightning Payment Service generates invoice
%% 4. LND node creates BOLT11 payment request
%% 5. Invoice stored in database
%% 6. Real-time notification sent to user

sequenceDiagram
    actor Creator as Content Creator
    participant UI as Frontend UI
    participant API as API Gateway
    participant Auth as Auth Middleware
    participant LPS as Lightning Payment Service
    participant PSM as Payment State Machine
    participant LND as LND Node
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Database
    participant Cache as Redis Cache
    participant WS as WebSocket Service

    Note over Creator,WS: Invoice Creation Flow - BOLT11 Generation

    %% Step 1: User Request
    Creator->>UI: Request payment for content
    Note over Creator,UI: Amount: 1000 sats<br/>Description: "Premium Article"

    UI->>API: POST /api/payments/create-invoice
    Note over UI,API: Body: {<br/>  amount_msats: 1000000,<br/>  description: "Premium Article",<br/>  content_id: "abc123"<br/>}

    %% Step 2: Authentication
    API->>Auth: Validate JWT token
    Auth->>Auth: Check user permissions

    alt Invalid Token
        Auth-->>API: 401 Unauthorized
        API-->>UI: Error: Invalid credentials
        UI-->>Creator: Show login prompt
    end

    Auth-->>API: User authenticated ✓
    Note over Auth,API: user_id: "user-uuid"

    %% Step 3: Validation
    API->>API: Validate request data
    API->>API: Check rate limits (100/min)
    API->>API: Validate amount (min 1 sat)

    alt Validation Failed
        API-->>UI: 400 Bad Request
        UI-->>Creator: Show error message
    end

    %% Step 4: Lightning Invoice Generation
    API->>LPS: createInvoice(user_id, amount, description)

    LPS->>LPS: Generate unique payment_hash
    Note over LPS: SHA256(randomBytes(32))

    LPS->>Cache: Check for duplicate invoice
    Cache-->>LPS: No duplicate found ✓

    LPS->>LND: addInvoice(amount_msats, description, expiry)
    Note over LPS,LND: RPC: addInvoice<br/>Amount: 1000000 msats<br/>Expiry: 3600 seconds (1 hour)

    LND->>LND: Generate BOLT11 invoice
    LND->>LND: Sign with node private key
    LND-->>LPS: Invoice created ✓
    Note over LND,LPS: payment_request: "lnbc10m1..."<br/>payment_hash: "abc123..."<br/>expires_at: timestamp

    %% Step 5: Database Storage
    LPS->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION

    LPS->>DB: INSERT INTO payments
    Note over LPS,DB: {<br/>  id: UUID,<br/>  user_id: "user-uuid",<br/>  payment_hash: "abc123...",<br/>  payment_request: "lnbc10m1...",<br/>  amount_msats: 1000000,<br/>  status: "PENDING",<br/>  expires_at: timestamp,<br/>  metadata: {...}<br/>}

    DB-->>LPS: Payment record created ✓

    %% Step 6: State Machine Initialization
    LPS->>PSM: initialize(payment_id, PENDING)
    PSM->>DB: INSERT INTO payment_events
    Note over PSM,DB: {<br/>  payment_id: UUID,<br/>  event: "INVOICE_CREATED",<br/>  from_state: null,<br/>  to_state: "PENDING",<br/>  timestamp: now()<br/>}

    DB-->>PSM: Event logged ✓
    PSM-->>LPS: State initialized ✓

    LPS->>DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
    DB-->>LPS: Transaction committed ✓

    %% Step 7: Caching
    LPS->>Cache: SET invoice:payment_hash, invoice_data
    Note over LPS,Cache: TTL: 3600 seconds<br/>(matches invoice expiry)
    Cache-->>LPS: Cached ✓

    %% Step 8: Response
    LPS-->>API: Invoice created successfully
    Note over LPS,API: {<br/>  id: UUID,<br/>  payment_request: "lnbc10m1...",<br/>  payment_hash: "abc123...",<br/>  amount_msats: 1000000,<br/>  expires_at: timestamp,<br/>  status: "PENDING"<br/>}

    API-->>UI: 201 Created + invoice data

    UI->>UI: Generate QR code from BOLT11
    UI->>UI: Display payment details

    %% Step 9: Real-time Setup
    UI->>WS: Subscribe to payment updates
    Note over UI,WS: channel: "payment:abc123..."
    WS-->>UI: Subscribed ✓

    UI-->>Creator: Show invoice + QR code
    Note over Creator,UI: ✓ Invoice ready for payment<br/>✓ 1000 sats (1000000 msats)<br/>✓ Expires in 1 hour<br/>✓ QR code displayed

    %% Step 10: Background Monitoring
    Note over LPS,DB: Invoice monitoring begins<br/>Retry service watches for payment<br/>Expiration service schedules cleanup
